%I A401732 #7 Nov 09 2026 23:26:33
%S A401732 1,2,10,15,225,5005,25050025,4340324450
%N A401732 Numbers k with no p^p-factors, such that A083345(k) is equal to A276085(k), where A083345 is the numerator of the fully additive function with a(p) = 1/p, and A276085 is fully additive with a(p) = p#/p.
%C A401732 As this is the sequence A276086(A401731(.)) sorted into ascending order, we know that also the following terms are also present: 125375375125, 627503752500625, 2803555083732433030, 48461452161660628090, 837690815937276571270, 14480084104058637874810, 250298596655870740407430, 216194668706246201133688649383063650, thus this is a proper subsequence of A401730 as at least the terms 50726876775575, 2840027504167937996637725, 135730131917554591054606843875 in that sequence are not present in this one. However, it is still not known where this differs from A401730 for the first time.
%H A401732 <a href="/index/Pri#primorial_numbers">Index entries for sequences related to primorial numbers</a>.
%o A401732 (PARI)
%o A401732 A083345(n) = { my(f=factor(n)); numerator(vecsum(vector(#f~, i, f[i, 2]/f[i, 1]))); };
%o A401732 A276085(n) = { my(f = factor(n)); sum(k=1, #f~, f[k, 2]*prod(i=1, primepi(f[k, 1]-1), prime(i))); };
%o A401732 A359550(n) = { my(pp); forprime(p=2, , pp = p^p; if(!(n%pp), return(0)); if(pp > n, return(1))); };
%o A401732 is_A401732(n) = (A359550(n) && A276085(n) == A083345(n));
%Y A401732 Cf. A083345, A276085.
%Y A401732 Intersection of A401730 and A401935.
%Y A401732 Subsequence of A048103.
%Y A401732 Cf. also A373484, A373485, A369650.
%K A401732 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401732 1,2
%A A401732 _Antti Karttunen_, Nov 09 2026
